# Demo Rule — Apply to Specific Files (JSON Schema)

This rule applies when editing the mental models JSON data (especially `data/mental-models.json`).

## Required schema (per object)
- id: string (unique, stable)
- title: string
- shortDescription: 1–2 sentences
- detailedExplanation: array of strings (bullet points)
- relatedFeatures: array of strings
- docs: array of objects: { label, url }

## Quality checks
- Keep JSON strictly valid (double quotes, no trailing commas).
- Keep formatting readable (consistent indentation).
- Use consistent casing and naming style across objects.
- Prefer 5–8 mental models with distinct, non-overlapping ideas.
